    "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer planar dielectric thin film stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer materials alternate between HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand), starting with HfO2 at the air side. Optimize the individual thickness of each of the 24 layers to maximize transmittance in the 1530-1565 nm wavelength band while maximizing reflectance in the 400-700 nm wavelength band. Each layer thickness is an independent variable constrained between 20 nm and 400 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimization with global perturbation amplitude of 5 nm. Apply uniform initialization weights across all 24 layers (no asymmetric weighting on layers 3 or 6). Include a phase-jump repair step: at each optimization round, randomly select 10% of the candidate population and apply stochastic thickness offsets of ±50 nm to forcibly cross local interference minima before resuming gradient refinement. Total layer count is fixed at exactly 24 layers. Materials are HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) only. Substrate is fused silica. Incident medium is air. Evaluate performance using frequency-domain plane-wave illumination at normal incidence.",
